.TH KVASIR-NODE 1 2026-11-20 Kvasir "Kvasir"
.SH NAME
kvasir-node \- a Kvasir database node, serving the MySQL protocol
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kvasir-node
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-listen
.IR HOST ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-tls-certificate
.IR PEM ]
.RB [ \-\-tls-key
.IR PEM ]
.RB [ \-\-ack-level
.IR LEVEL ]
.RB [ \-\-user
.IR NAME : CREDENTIAL ]...
.br
.B kvasir-node hash-password
.br
.B kvasir-node \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kvasir-node
is one node of Kvasir, a MySQL-compatible relational database. Any MySQL 8.4
client, driver or tool connects to it; clients sign in with
.B caching_sha2_password
only after TLS.
.PP
This release keeps its databases in memory: nothing is written to disk, and a
node does not yet join other nodes. Everything committed is lost when the node
stops, which is the promise of the
.B ephemeral
acknowledgement level, the only one this release starts at.
.PP
SIGINT or SIGTERM stops the node.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B hash-password
Reads one line, a password, from standard input and prints a credential for
.BR \-\-user .
.SH OPTIONS
Every option is also a key in the settings file, in
.B secrets.yaml
beside it, or an environment variable; an option wins over the variable, and
the variable over the file.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
The settings file (YAML). Otherwise
.BR $KVASIR_CONFIG ,
else
.I /etc/kvasir/config.yaml
when it exists.
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " HOST"
The address to listen on (key
.BR listen.host ,
.BR $KVASIR_LISTEN );
0.0.0.0 by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
The port (key
.BR listen.port ,
.BR $KVASIR_PORT );
3306 by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-tls-certificate " PEM"
The node's certificate chain (key
.BR tls.certificate ,
.BR $KVASIR_TLS_CERTIFICATE ).
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-tls-key " PEM"
The node's private key (key
.BR tls.key ,
.BR $KVASIR_TLS_KEY ).
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-ack-level " LEVEL"
How far a commit has gone before the client is answered (key
.BR ack_level ,
.BR $KVASIR_ACK_LEVEL ).
Required, with no built-in default; this release accepts only
.BR ephemeral .
.TP
.BI \-\-user " NAME" : CREDENTIAL
An account (key
.BR users ,
a list); at least one is required.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Prints the version and exits.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/kvasir/config.yaml
The settings.
.TP
.I /etc/kvasir/secrets.yaml
The accounts, readable by the node's user alone.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when stopped by a signal; 2 for settings that cannot be used; 1 for any other
failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mysql (1)
